# ── Database (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development:
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/adwuma360?schema=public"
# Serverless hosting (Vercel etc.): use your provider's POOLED connection string
# and require TLS, otherwise concurrent requests will exhaust Postgres connections.
#   postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DB?sslmode=require
# Do NOT add ?connection_limit= or ?pgbouncer= — those are Prisma query-engine
# flags and are ignored by the pg driver adapter this app uses. Pool size is a
# driver option instead; override it with DATABASE_POOL_MAX below.

# Connections per instance. Defaults to 1 on Vercel and 10 elsewhere.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX="1"

# ── Auth (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET="generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32"
AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"          # set to your deployment origin in production
AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true

# Optional: Google sign-in. The button only appears when BOTH are set, so
# leaving these blank simply omits it rather than showing a control that fails.
#
# From console.cloud.google.com: APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create
# credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application. The authorised redirect
# URI must be exactly, one line per origin you use:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#   https://your-domain/api/auth/callback/google
#
# Only an address Google has verified is accepted, and a first sign-in creates
# the account and sends them to /onboarding to name their business.
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=""
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=""

# ── App (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for metadata and for the links in verification / password-reset emails.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Branding (all optional — defaults live in src/lib/config/brand.ts) ───────
NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME="Adwuma360"
NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_SHORT_NAME="Adwuma360"
# The two brand hues are sampled from the logomark and live in
# src/lib/config/brand.ts. Set these only to re-theme a white-label build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_PRIMARY="#2563eb"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_SECONDARY="#0c3060"
NEXT_PUBLIC_COUNTRY="Ghana"
NEXT_PUBLIC_COUNTRY_CODE="GH"
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_TAX_RATE="10"
# Currency is read by every money formatter in the app. Changing it relabels
# existing figures rather than converting them, so only set it on a workspace
# whose records are already in that currency.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CURRENCY="GHS"
NEXT_PUBLIC_CURRENCY_SYMBOL="GH₵"

# ── Email ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "console" (the default) sends nothing and prints the message, including the
# confirmation code and any link, to the server log. Every flow is testable
# that way: the confirmation screen says where the code came out rather than
# telling people to check an inbox that will stay empty.
# There is no package to install — Resend is called over its HTTPS API.
# See docs/EMAIL.md, and `npm run email:preview` to read the templates.
EMAIL_TRANSPORT="console"

# "resend" delivers over HTTPS, which is what a serverless host can do —
# outbound SMTP ports are usually closed, so an SMTP client would just hang.
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT="resend"
# RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."

# Must be an address on a domain verified with the provider. Until you verify
# one, Resend accepts onboarding@resend.dev and will only deliver to the email
# address that owns the Resend account.
EMAIL_FROM="Adwuma360 <support@adwuma360.online>"

# ── Payments (Paystack) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave every one of these blank and the product still works: the billing page
# records a plan request and says someone will be in touch, which is what it
# did before payments existed. Nothing shows a checkout it cannot complete.
#
# The secret key. Server only — it is never sent to the browser, and the file
# that uses it is marked `server-only` so importing it into a client component
# is a build error rather than a leak.
#   sk_test_... while you are testing, sk_live_... when you are charging people
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=""
#
# One plan code per plan and period, from Paystack -> Plans -> Create Plan.
# A plan with no code here is not purchasable and falls back to the request
# route, which is how Enterprise behaves by design.
#
# Two rules for the plans you create there:
#   - Currency must be GHS, matching PLATFORM_CURRENCY in src/lib/config/plans.ts
#   - The amount must equal the price shown for that plan in the same file
# The checkout reads the live plan and refuses if the two disagree, rather than
# charging a figure nobody was shown. If a "Subscribe" button says the plan is
# mid-update, that mismatch is what it means.
#
# Interval: Monthly for the _MONTHLY codes, Annually for the _ANNUAL ones.
# PAYSTACK_PLAN_STARTER_MONTHLY="PLN_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
# PAYSTACK_PLAN_STARTER_ANNUAL="PLN_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
# PAYSTACK_PLAN_BUSINESS_MONTHLY="PLN_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
# PAYSTACK_PLAN_BUSINESS_ANNUAL="PLN_xxxxxxxxxxxx"
#
# Enterprise is priced per customer and normally has no plan code. Set these
# only if you create a standard Enterprise plan you are happy to sell online.
# PAYSTACK_PLAN_ENTERPRISE_MONTHLY=""
# PAYSTACK_PLAN_ENTERPRISE_ANNUAL=""
#
# Finally, in Paystack -> Settings -> API Keys & Webhooks, set the webhook URL:
#   https://your-domain/api/webhooks/paystack
# That webhook, not the page the customer comes back to, is what marks a
# workspace as paid. It is signed with the secret key above and verified before
# anything is read, so it needs no separate secret of its own.

# ── Search engines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Proves to Google Search Console that you own the site. Paste only the value
# from the meta tag, not the whole tag:
#   <meta name="google-site-verification" content="THIS_PART_ONLY">
# Not a secret: it is published in the page source by design. Adwuma360's own
# token is the built-in default, so this only needs setting on a fork or a
# second brand. Whatever is verified must stay put, because Google re-checks it
# and un-verifies a site that drops it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=""

# The same for Bing Webmaster Tools, if you use it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=""

# ── Operating Adwuma360 itself ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Addresses listed here can open the operator console at /admin, whatever the
# database says. It is the bootstrap: a fresh deployment has no operator, and
# something has to be able to create the first one. It is also the way back in
# if the last operator flag is revoked by mistake.
#
# Everyone else is granted from inside the console, which sets a flag on the
# account. Neither route grants anything inside a customer's workspace.
#
# Comma separated. Leave empty in an environment nobody should be operating
# the platform from.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS=""

# Whole domains, so everyone at the company is staff without being added one
# at a time. Bare domains, comma separated: adwuma360.online
#
# Unlike the list above, this one only counts once the address has been
# confirmed by email. It is a wildcard, and anyone can type an address into the
# registration form: requiring confirmation means they had to receive the
# message, so they really do hold the address. Subdomains are not included,
# because whoever runs mail.example.com does not necessarily run example.com.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_DOMAINS=""
